  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> denotes centroid, circumcentre and orthocentre respectively.</p><p>We know that, the line joining orthocentre and circumcentre is divided by centroid in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, where distance from orthocentre being the larger part.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/926113ca-80c9-4c7d-80cb-322f7405bfac.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 97px;\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>≡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>7</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>≡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Distance from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> measured along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi></math></p><p>Where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So, the distance of point from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>17</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>·</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>·</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>17</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
